% p23_num_shift -- discriminates SHIFTING past a numeral. Inferring `var 0`
% shifts its context type `Q 7` by 1; a numeral must come back UNCHANGED.
% If k_shift treated tag 7 as a var or as a two-field node the copy would
% differ from the written type and conversion would fail, so acceptance here
% is the shift rule, not a coincidence.
0 sort 0
axiom I64 : 0
numtype I64
1 const I64
2 sort 0
3 pi 1 2
axiom Q : 3
4 const Q
5 num 7
6 app 4 5
7 var 0
8 lam 6 7
9 const Q
10 num 7
11 app 9 10
12 const Q
13 num 7
14 app 12 13
15 pi 11 14
check 8 : 15
